Project scope
-------------

qisiTV is a local-first, single-user workspace for AI-assisted video
creation. The web-engine edition uses a browser React interface and a paired
Go backend listening on loopback; the desktop edition uses Wails. Projects, canvas state,
generated assets, model-channel settings, and durable task state are stored in
the user's local workspace. Requests leave the device only when a user invokes
an externally configured model provider or another explicitly networked tool.

